lest two-digit primes, we get:\n     \\[\n     5 \\times 11 \\times 13 = 5 \\times 143 = 715\n     \\]\n   - If we use the next smallest one-digit prime, which is 7, and the two smallest two-digit primes, we get:\n     \\[\n     7 \\times 11 \\times 13 = 7 \\times 143 = 1001\n     \\]\n\n   From these calculations, we can see that the smallest product is when we use the one-digit prime 2 and the two-digit primes 11 and 13.\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible product of one one-digit prime and two distinct two-digit primes is \\(\\boxed{286}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{286}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:471"}
